Mythbeast Survivors

An offline, single-player, portrait 2D survivor game built with Godot and
GDScript. Fight through Whispering Grove, a woodland arena featuring an
original chibi adventurer, soft forest scenery, and local audio.

Getting started

  Install Godot 4.7.2 Standard.
  In the Godot Project Manager, import project.godot from this directory.
  Press F5, select Play, and start Whispering Grove on Normal.

  The main menu opens Permanent Upgrades, Settings, and Credits. Settings
  saves music, sound effects, and Reduced Effects on this device. Move
  with WASD or the arrow keys on desktop. On a touchscreen, press and
  drag below the HUD. Release to stop. Use Pause or Esc to pause.

Whispering Grove

  Survive three escalating waves of Forest Slimes, Swift Fanglings, and Moss
  Golems. Your hero casts Arcane Bolt automatically. Collect XP crystals to
  choose among six run upgrades. Pause and upgrade selection freeze the clock.
  At 03:00, defeat the Ancient Grove Beast to win. Move out of the circular
  stomp or the charge lane before the warning resolves. Play Again starts a
  fresh run after victory, and Try Again restarts after defeat.

  Enemy silhouettes, color-coded ability effects, and short damage numbers
  help you read the fight. The Grove and its boss have separate music.
  Reduced Effects limits extra particles, damage accents, and camera motion
  while keeping attack warnings and ability areas visible.

  Victories and qualifying defeats earn Star Essence. Spend it on permanent
  health, magic damage, or movement upgrades. Clearing Normal unlocks Hard.
  The local save keeps your progress, records, and settings. Crystal
  Caverns is shown as Coming Soon.

Native test builds

  The Android Debug preset builds an ARM64 APK for Android 7.0 (API 24)
  or later. Configure the Java 17 and Android SDK paths in Godot's
  Editor Settings under Export > Android. With the matching Godot export
  templates installed, run:

    bash scripts/build-android-debug.sh

  The script verifies the APK signature, alignment, package identity, and
  manifest permissions. The APK is written to
  build/android/MythbeastSurvivors-debug.apk. The package identifier is
  io.github.bradyworld2024.mythbeastsurvivors.

  The iOS preset uses the same app identity and version. On macOS
  with Xcode, set GODOT_IOS_TEAM_ID to your Apple team and run
  bash scripts/export-ios.sh to generate an Xcode project. Xcode manages
  development signing and iPhone deployment separately.

Project layout

  core/app          Application entry, scene navigation, and audio lifetime
  features          Native level, combat, progression, enemies, and boss
  ui                Menus, HUD, safe-area layout, and shared theme
  data              Levels, waves, combat, rewards, difficulty, and upgrades
  assets            Project artwork, application icon, and audio
  tests/smoke       Foundation navigation and behavior checks

Development checks

  Run these commands from this directory. Set GODOT_BIN if the executable
  is installed outside PATH.

    bash scripts/test-godot.sh --gate
    bash scripts/test-godot.sh

  The required gate runs a curated set of startup, navigation, movement,
  combat, progression, survival, persistent replay, and combat feedback
  checks. CI also checks the native build scripts' shell syntax. The second
  command runs every smoke suite, including audio, touch layout,
  save recovery, and purchase failure handling. Both isolate test profiles
  from the player's save.
  Add critical regressions to the gate when related behavior changes.

